{"name":"Draw Your Sword","hex":"#6c7179","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"draw","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Senses relating to exerting force or pulling.\n To pull (someone or something) in a particular direction or manner. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To pull (someone or something) in a particular direction or manner. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Pull back your bowstring in preparation to shoot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/draw"},{"term":"your","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Determiner","definitions":["Belonging to you; of you; related to you (singular; one owner).","Belonging to you; of you; related to you (plural; more owners)."]},{"part":"Contraction","definitions":["Misspelling of you're."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/your"},{"term":"sword","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together forming a hilt), which is designed to cut, stab, slash and/or hack.","A suit in certain playing card decks, particularly those used in Spain and Italy, or those used for divination.\nA card of this suit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stab or cut with a sword"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword"}],"entries":[{"title":"You","blocks":[{"text":"In Modern English, the word \"you\" is the second-person pronoun. It is grammatically plural, and was historically used only for the dative case, but in most modern dialects is used for all cases and numbers."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You","wikidata":"Q1165897"},{"title":"Sword","blocks":[{"text":"A sword is an edged, bladed weapon intended for manual cutting or thrusting. Its blade, longer than that of a knife or dagger, is attached to a hilt and can be straight or curved. A thrusting sword tends to have a straighter blade with a pointed tip. A slashing sword is more likely to be curved and to have a sharpened cutting edge on one or both sides of the blade. Many swords are designed for both thrusting and slashing. The precise definition of a sword varies by historical epoch and geographic region."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sword","wikidata":"Q12791"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swiss longsword, 15th or 16th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspadon-Morges.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/1280px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Western Han iron sword","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWestern_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Apa_Schwerter.jpg/500px-Apa_Schwerter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Apa_Schwerter.jpg/500px-Apa_Schwerter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Apa-type swords, 17th-century BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApa_Schwerter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikiped